From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:39:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] usb: mtu3: drop the pullup for a suspend taken with no host
 session

On the Gemini the PHY forces the B session valid, so the gadget stays
pulled up with the cable out. After a resume that reconnected the
gadget with no cable attached, a second system suspend half a second
later failed: the IP did not report sleep within 100 ms ("ip sleep
failed!!!") and the suspend returned -EBUSY. With a host session that
was then lost to an unplug, the bus suspends and the IP sleeps as
expected.

When the gadget is pulled up but has no host session, take D+ down for
the suspend and restore it at resume. The driver already treats a
device that is not pulled up as one whose IP is not expected to sleep:
it skips the wait and powers the PHY and clocks down. A session that
the bus suspended keeps its pullup, as before.
---
 drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3.h      |  1 +
 drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_core.c | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 27 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3.h b/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3.h
index 597bb4b49..93e644af5 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3.h
+++ b/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3.h
@@ -369,6 +369,7 @@ struct mtu3 {
 	unsigned connected:1;
 	unsigned bus_suspended:1;
 	unsigned reconnect_on_resume:1;
+	unsigned pullup_off_in_suspend:1;
 	unsigned async_callbacks:1;
 	unsigned separate_fifo:1;
 
diff --git a/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_core.c b/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_core.c
index 2b8f38617..5d091dc44 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_core.c
@@ -1023,7 +1023,7 @@ bool ssusb_gadget_ip_sleep_check(struct ssusb_mtk *ssusb)
 		return true;
 
 	/* device is started and pullup D+, ip can sleep */
-	if (mtu->is_active && mtu->softconnect)
+	if (mtu->is_active && mtu->softconnect && !mtu->pullup_off_in_suspend)
 		return true;
 
 	/* ip can't sleep if not pullup D+ when support device mode */
@@ -1051,6 +1051,21 @@ int ssusb_gadget_suspend(struct ssusb_mtk *ssusb, pm_message_t msg)
 	 */
 	mtu->reconnect_on_resume = mtu->connected;
 
+	/*
+	 * Pulled up with no host session since, as after a pullup with the
+	 * cable out where the PHY forces the session valid, the IP does not
+	 * report sleep. Take D+ down for the suspend instead, the state in
+	 * which the IP is not expected to sleep, and put it back at resume.
+	 */
+	if (!mtu->connected && mtu->is_active && mtu->softconnect) {
+		unsigned long flags;
+
+		spin_lock_irqsave(&mtu->lock, flags);
+		mtu3_dev_on_off(mtu, 0);
+		mtu->pullup_off_in_suspend = 1;
+		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&mtu->lock, flags);
+	}
+
 	mtu3_dev_suspend(mtu);
 	synchronize_irq(mtu->irq);
 
@@ -1066,6 +1081,16 @@ int ssusb_gadget_resume(struct ssusb_mtk *ssusb, pm_message_t msg)
 
 	mtu3_dev_resume(mtu);
 
+	if (mtu->pullup_off_in_suspend) {
+		unsigned long flags;
+
+		spin_lock_irqsave(&mtu->lock, flags);
+		mtu->pullup_off_in_suspend = 0;
+		if (mtu->is_active && mtu->softconnect)
+			mtu3_dev_on_off(mtu, 1);
+		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&mtu->lock, flags);
+	}
+
 	/*
 	 * The power-down dropped the link and the D+ pullup, so the host has
 	 * to enumerate the device afresh: report the disconnect that a VBUS
-- 
2.43.0

